Task 1: Install and Configure OTP using ipa otptoken-add
Subtask 1.1: Understanding OTP Token Types
FreeIPA supports two main types of OTP tokens:

HOTP (HMAC-based One-Time Password): Counter-based tokens
TOTP (Time-based One-Time Password): Time-based tokens (most common)
Subtask 1.2: Create a TOTP Token
Step 1: Generate a Basic TOTP Token

# Create a TOTP token for user testuser
ipa otptoken-add --type=totp --desc="Test User Mobile Token"

# The command will output a QR code and secret key
# Save the secret key for manual entry if needed
Step 2: Create a Named TOTP Token

# Create a token with a specific identifier
ipa otptoken-add testuser-mobile \
  --type=totp \
  --desc="Test User Mobile Device" \
  --algo=sha1 \
  --digits=6 \
  --interval=30
Expected Output:

Added OTP token "testuser-mobile"
  Unique ID: testuser-mobile
  Type: TOTP
  Description: Test User Mobile Device
  Algorithm: sha1
  Digits: 6
  Clock interval: 30
  URI: otpauth://totp/testuser@example.com?secret=ABCD...&issuer=example.com
Subtask 1.3: Create an HOTP Token
# Create an HOTP (counter-based) token
ipa otptoken-add testuser-hotp \
  --type=hotp \
  --desc="Test User Hardware Token" \
  --algo=sha1 \
  --digits=6 \
  --counter=1
Subtask 1.4: View Token Information
# List all OTP tokens
ipa otptoken-find

# Show specific token details
ipa otptoken-show testuser-mobile

# Display QR code for token (if needed again)
ipa otptoken-show testuser-mobile --show-uri
Task 2: Enroll a User for OTP
Subtask 2.1: Create a Test User
Step 1: Create a New User Account

# Create a test user for OTP enrollment
ipa user-add testuser \
  --first=Test \
  --last=User \
  --email=testuser@example.com \
  --password
Step 2: Verify User Creation

# Confirm user was created successfully
ipa user-show testuser

# Check user's authentication methods
ipa user-show testuser --all
Subtask 2.2: Assign OTP Token to User
Step 1: Associate Token with User

# Assign the TOTP token to the user
ipa otptoken-mod testuser-mobile --owner=testuser

# Verify token assignment
ipa otptoken-show testuser-mobile
Step 2: Configure User for Two-Factor Authentication

# Enable two-factor authentication for the user
ipa user-mod testuser --user-auth-type=otp

# Verify the authentication type change
ipa user-show testuser --all | grep "User authentication types"
