Troubleshooting Common Issues
Issue 1: Time Synchronization Problems
Symptoms: OTP codes not working despite correct entry

Solution:

# Check time synchronization
sudo chrony sources -v

# Force time sync if needed
sudo chrony makestep

# Restart chronyd service
sudo systemctl restart chronyd
Issue 2: Token Not Associated with User
Symptoms: User cannot use OTP for authentication

Solution:

# Verify token ownership
ipa otptoken-find --owner=testuser

# Re-assign token if necessary
ipa otptoken-mod token-id --owner=testuser
Issue 3: SSH Authentication Failing
Symptoms: SSH not prompting for OTP

Solution:

# Check SSH configuration
sudo sshd -T | grep -i challenge

# Verify PAM configuration
sudo cat /etc/pam.d/sshd | grep pam_sss

# Check SSH logs
sudo journalctl -u sshd -f
Issue 4: Web Interface Not Accepting OTP
Symptoms: Web login fails with correct credentials and OTP

Solution:

# Check IPA services
sudo ipactl status

# Restart IPA services if needed
sudo ipactl restart

# Check web server logs
sudo journalctl -u httpd -f
Advanced Configuration Options
Custom Token Parameters
# Create token with custom parameters
ipa otptoken-add advanced-token \
  --type=totp \
  --desc="Advanced Configuration Token" \
  --algo=sha256 \
  --digits=8 \
  --interval=60 \
  --owner=testuser
Bulk Token Management
# Create multiple tokens for different users
for user in user1 user2 user3; do
  ipa otptoken-add ${user}-token \
    --type=totp \
    --desc="Token for $user" \
    --owner=$user
done
Token Policies and Restrictions
# Set token usage policies
ipa otptoken-mod testuser-mobile \
  --desc="Mobile token - restricted to business hours"

# View all token policies
ipa otptoken-find --all
Security Best Practices
Token Management Guidelines
Regular Token Rotation

# Disable old tokens
ipa otptoken-del old-token-id

# Create new tokens periodically
ipa otptoken-add new-token --owner=user
Monitor Token Usage

# Check authentication logs
sudo journalctl -u sssd -f | grep OTP

# Monitor failed authentication attempts
sudo tail -f /var/log/secure | grep authentication
Backup and Recovery

# Export token information (for backup)
ipa otptoken-find --all > otp-tokens-backup.txt

# Create emergency access tokens
ipa otptoken-add emergency-$(date +%Y%m%d) --type=hotp
